 :protocol {:states [:disconnected :awaiting-subscription :pre-fence :snapshot :post-fence :awaiting-admission :fresh-at-cut :uncertain]
            :cut "Attempt with generation g, bounded deadline and distinct unpredictable per-attempt pre/post nonces. After successful subscription acknowledgement for window/workspace plus tick events, send pre tick and consume its matching first=false event on the SAME serialized subscribed stream. Only then request GET_TREE; wait for its sanitized bounded result, then send post tick and consume matching event on that stream. A clean attempt has no relevant structural notification, decode failure, overflow, disconnect, generation change or unaccounted event between the two matched fences; otherwise discard candidate and retry only within bounded attempts/deadline. Pre fence drains earlier stream notifications; post fence drains notifications generated before SEND_TICK. Tick command replies and initial/unmatched ticks cannot substitute."
            :proof-obligation "The above is a candidate protocol, not a proof of atomic GET_TREE or complete notification coverage. Qualify only if an exact-version owner-backed justification covers snapshot processing, stream FIFO and all relevant structural changes, and the edge serializes receipt without hidden buffering. If any guarantee is absent or a structural change can be silent, remain uncertain; do not equate quiet tick interval with proof. A post-fence event after clean publication immediately revokes the local lease and refreshes; if it exposes an earlier generated event or sequencing ambiguity, invalidate the prior cut claim and record a historical gap. Never retroactively claim certainty."
            :admission "Construct S2A-valid baseline or gap/reconciled-baseline only after justified clean cut; submit through injected admission seam with exact candidate identity, revision, lease and generation. On failure, timeout, stale generation/head or changed event stream while pending, no current publication. Acceptance alone cannot revive an expired cut. Test replay via actual frozen law and actual Clio canonical owner where permitted, not a cloned validator."
            :boundedness "Explicit fixed limits for bytes, JSON depth/nodes, tree/window count, queue size, nonce size, attempts and elapsed duration; choose and document concrete constants in reviewed implementation. Reject before allocation/traversal wherever possible, drain no unbounded queue, do not retain raw payload or exception. Exhaustion, malformed frames, unsupported event, unknown ordering or continuing churn produces finite denial/uncertainty, no silent retries."
            :identity "Generation changes on any request/event channel loss, overflow, replaced source or ambiguous continuity; invalidate leases and all outstanding callbacks before resubscribe. Key windows by server epoch + XID + new incarnation UUID. A close/reuse within epoch requires a fresh incarnation; a gap invalidates continuity even when XID and content match. Preserve old memberships as history; never reassign them. A gap/reconciliation follows frozen desktop semantics and direct causal references, not invented intermediate observations."
            :sanitization "Allowlist only synthetic structural node/window IDs, parent relation, allowed geometry and synthetic workspace identifiers required for validated projection. Never retain or emit titles, window names, application names/classes, marks, raw JSON, arbitrary strings, environment, socket paths or personal content. Stable IDs and hashes may themselves identify resources: only controlled synthetic sources are admissible. Reject malformed/unknown/over-limit structures; bound values and logs. Do not use operator windows even as test data."}
